From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: store and cache defaults: device removal, message
 cache, profile pictures, group names

* Remove only the deleted account's device from the store

All WhatsApp accounts share whatsmeow.db. When an account is deleted
("account-removed"), its device is logged out if a client is still
connected, otherwise its row is deleted from the store by the device
JID in its credentials. The other accounts stay linked.

* Keep a message cache by default

Replies, reactions and poll votes look up their target in the message
cache, which defaults to 0 messages (off). Default it to 500, and use
500 when the stored setting is 0.

* Fetch profile pictures by default and restore lost ones

webOS shows contact pictures, so "preview" is the default (the first
choice of the list option and the fallback when unset). When a buddy has
no icon, its picture is requested without the stored picture id, so
whatsmeow sends it again instead of answering that it is unchanged.

* Fetch group names on connect

Group info was only queried when the room list was opened, so group
chats showed their raw JID. Query it on connect.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
